{"term":"oversee","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b53498052bf43c8149","definition":"To survey, look at something in a wide angle.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"literally","register":"literally, transitive","wordFamily":["overseer","oversight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oversee#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2f4b862f2b0e2fcdaa","definition":"To supervise, guide, review or direct the actions of a person or group.","example":"It is congress's duty to oversee the spending of federal funds.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["superintend"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["overseer","oversight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oversee#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:56c61cdd09a03ddfa8","definition":"To inspect, examine.","example":"Gamekeepers oversee a hunting ground to see to the wildlife's welfare and look for poachers.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overseer","oversight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oversee#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0de396e2c06e20856a","definition":"To fail to see; to overlook, ignore.","example":"Thereat the Elfe did blush in priuitee, / And turnd his face away; but she the same / Dissembled faire, and faynd to ouersee.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["overseer","oversight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktio